---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Editbar demo — Astro</title>
    <style>
      body {
        font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Inter", system-ui, sans-serif;
        max-width: 640px;
        margin: 10vh auto;
        padding: 0 24px;
        line-height: 1.5;
      }
      h1 { font-size: 2.25rem; }
      .note { margin-top: 48px; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.7; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1 data-edit-id="astro.title">Built with Astro, edited without code</h1>
    <p data-edit-id="astro.subtitle">
      This page is server-rendered to plain HTML at build time — data-edit-id
      survives that step unchanged, same as it survives React's or Vue's
      compiler.
    </p>
    <p data-edit-id="astro.body">
      No Astro-specific integration is used here — just the widget script
      tag, same as every other example.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Visit <a href="http://localhost:4000/setup">localhost:4000/setup</a> for
      your admin token and the exact link to open this page as an admin
      (make sure the reference server is running on port 4000) — the token
      is generated fresh per server, so there's no fixed one to hardcode.
    </p>
    <script src="http://localhost:4000/widget.js" data-api="http://localhost:4000" defer></script>
  </body>
</html>
